   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green Investments Partnership (GIP) is a blended finance credit fund managed by&#xfffd;Pentagreen&#xfffd;Capital, a fund manager established by HSBC and Temasek to drive&#xfffd;green&#xfffd;infrastructure&#xfffd;investments, fill a key climate finance funding gap in Southeast Asia, and mobilise commercial capital into the sector. GIP is a pillar of the Finance Asia&apos;s Transition&#xfffd;Partnership&#xfffd;(FAST-P), with GIP providing financing solutions for climate projects through senior loans, mezzanine finance, and subordinated debt. GIP aims to address the funding gap for projects that are on the cusp of bankability but have characteristics which make them challenging for traditional lenders to finance.</narrative>
   </description>
